  "problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\nI. The probability that an inbox with $100$ emails contains $45$ spam emails, given that the probability that a single email is spam is $0.47.$\n\nII. The probability that less than $2$ light bulbs are defective from a box containing $20$ lightbulbs if the probability of a single bulb being defective is $0.12.$\n\nIII. The probability of finding more than $16$ people with blood type A$-$ in a randomly selected sample of $50$ people, given that the probability that a randomly selected person has blood type A$-$ is $0.08.$",
